# Day 24

## Experiment Title

Working with Docker Volumes in Docker Compose


## Objective

To understand the use of Docker volumes for persistent data storage in Docker Compose applications.


## Theory

Docker volumes are used to store data permanently outside the container filesystem. They help in preserving application data even when containers are stopped or removed.

In Docker Compose, volumes can be defined inside the YAML configuration file and attached to containers easily. Volumes are commonly used with databases and applications that require persistent storage.

Using volumes improves data management and prevents data loss during container recreation.


## Requirements

Docker Desktop

Docker Compose

Windows Operating System


## Procedure

Open Docker Desktop and ensure that Docker services are running properly.

Create a Docker Compose configuration file withh volume settings.

Attach the volume to the required container service.

Start the Docker Compose application.

Verify that the Docker volume has been created successfully.

Stop and restart the containers to check data persistence.


## Output

Docker volume was created successfully using Docker Compose.

Application data remained stored even after restarting the containers.

Persistent storage was successfully implemented.


## Result

Successfully learned how to use Docker volumes for persistent storage in Docker Compose applications.
